cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  SCAN-Resources: Instruments and Training Datasets for the Synthetic
  Cognitive Augmentation Network
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Cite the version DOI for the release you actually used, not the concept
  DOI, so that the scoring model version is unambiguous.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Tate
    given-names: Levy
    alias: iLevyTate
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.14053202
    description: Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest version
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22598618
    description: Version DOI for 2.0.0 (instrument 2.0.0, scoring model 2.0.0; released 2026-09-07)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.16711302
    description: Version DOI for 1.1.0 (instrument 1.0.0, scoring model 1.0.0; released 2025-08-02)
repository-code: https://github.com/iLevyTate/SCAN-Resources
abstract: >-
  Resources for the Synthetic Cognitive Augmentation Network (SCAN): the
  SCANAQ alignment questionnaire and its scoring model, the CAUSE user
  survey, a generation prompt for synthetic training dialogues, and JSONL
  training and validation datasets for five prefrontal-cortex-simulating
  agents (DLPFC, VMPFC, OFC, ACC, MPFC).
keywords:
  - cognitive augmentation
  - prefrontal cortex
  - multi-agent systems
  - psychometrics
  - fine-tuning datasets
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
